   <text type="letter">
      <body>
         <div type="writingSession">
            <pb n="1"/>
            <opener><dateline>
                  <date when="1940-10-01">October 1 st. 40.</date></dateline><lb/>
               <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__931" type="person">Dr. Max Horkheimer.</rs><lb/>
               Institute of Social Research<lb/> 429 West 117 Street.<lb/>
               <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__319" type="place">New York City</rs>. <salute>Dear <rs
                     ref="#tillich_person_id__931" type="person">friend </rs>:</salute>
            </opener>
            <p><rs ref="#tillich_person_id__168" type="person">Dr. Maximilian Beck</rs> writes to me
               that his income in <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__767" type="place">Yale</rs> is only $
               80- monthly and that his son is without a scholarship in <rs
                  ref="#tillich_place_id__990" type="place">Cornell</rs>. He is very much concerned
               about his situation and asks you whether there is any chance to get help either in a
               form of a loan to be repaid not before two years or something like that. His address
               is: 225 Whitney Avenue, <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__770" type="place">New Haven,
                  Conn.</rs>
            </p><p> I would be very grateful if you could do something in this matter.</p>
            <closer>
               <salute>Very sincerely yours</salute>
               <signed><rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1928" type="person"
                  ><hi rend="hand">Paul Tillich</hi></rs></signed>
            </closer>
         </div>
      </body>
   </text>
